    "title_en": "Resolvable quantum Latin squares with maximal cardinality",
    "abstract_en": "A resolvable quantum Latin square of order $n$, denoted by $\\text{RQLS}(n)$, is a quantum Latin square admitting $n$ pairwise disjoint transversals. By employing complete mappings and extending the classical singular direct product construction to the quantum setting, we determine the existence of maximal-cardinality $\\text{RQLS}(n)$s with $17$ possible exceptions.",
